# NC Disaster Recovery Portal

> Official State of North Carolina portal for disaster recovery. Residents can check verified emergency alerts, view live county power outages, find recovery resources, apply for disaster assistance, and check the status of a request.

The portal is the public theme layer for North Carolina government disaster-recovery content. The pages below are the primary anonymous, publicly indexable entry points; the complete URL list (including CMS content pages) is at https://www.nc.gov/sitemap.xml.

## Key pages

- [Home](https://www.nc.gov/): Portal home and disaster-recovery landing page.
- [Disaster Support](https://www.nc.gov/disaster): Disaster Support hub linking alerts, resources, assistance, and status.
- [Alerts and Warnings](https://www.nc.gov/disaster/alerts): Verified emergency alerts and warnings from official agencies.
- [Current Power Outages](https://www.nc.gov/disaster/current-power-outages): Live power-outage information for North Carolina counties.
- [Latest Updates](https://www.nc.gov/disaster/latest-updates): Latest disaster recovery news and updates.
- [Recovery Resources](https://www.nc.gov/disaster/resources): Directory of recovery resources — food, benefits, health, housing, and more.
- [Request Assistance](https://www.nc.gov/disaster/support-request): Apply for disaster recovery assistance from North Carolina.
- [Employee Directory](https://www.nc.gov/employee-directory): Search the North Carolina state employee directory.
